      "message": "I can see change 535901 (the SHA1 referenced here), but I’m still trying to fully understand the intent behind this change.\n\nIn that change, the `gerrit_plugin` version is synchronized with the version in Gerrit core, and the commit message says:\n\n```\nThis change adapts the gerrit_plugin.bzl file to the version in Gerrit\ncore and makes it usable for in-tree builds of plugins.\n```\n\nIn the current change, though, it doesn’t look like the in-tree `tools/bzl/plugin.bzl` is being updated. Instead, it seems like we’re primarily pulling in `bazlets` to obtain the Gerrit Plugin-API version. Is that a fair understanding?\n\nIf so, it might be helpful to call that out explicitly in the commit message and briefly explain why this dependency is needed — that would make the motivation a lot clearer for reviewers.\n\nAlternatively, would it make sense to bring in the bazlets Plugin-API version (together with `bazlets/gerrit_plugin.bzl`) in a separate change, so this one can stay a bit more focused?",
